# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

A durable agent service on [DBOS](https://docs.dbos.dev/python/). Every model call and tool
call is a checkpointed step, so a crashed or redeployed run resumes where it stopped — **one
model call per step, one side effect per action** — instead of starting over.

## Quickstart

```bash
{%- if database == 'postgres' %}
docker compose up -d              # local Postgres for DBOS (or: dex run db-up)
{%- else %}
cp .env.example .env              # fill in LAKEBASE_* and Databricks auth
{%- endif %}
uv sync
uv run pytest                     # fake LLM, no API keys
uv run {{ project_name }} serve   # {% if include_api %}API + worker on :8000{% else %}queue worker{% endif %}
```

In another shell (set `{% if llm_sdk == 'openai' %}OPENAI_API_KEY{% else %}ANTHROPIC_API_KEY{% endif %}` for the server):

```bash
uv run {{ project_name }} run "record a note saying hello"   # prints a run id
{%- if include_hitl %}
uv run {{ project_name }} approve <run_id>                   # the example tool needs approval
{%- endif %}
uv run {{ project_name }} status <run_id>                    # state + step trace
```

## Crash demo

1. `uv run {{ project_name }} serve`, then start a run{% if include_hitl %} and approve it{% endif %}.
2. `kill -9` the server while the run is mid-tool-call.
3. Start `serve` again. DBOS recovers the run from its last completed step.
4. `status <run_id>` shows one `call_model` per turn and the ledger (`.effects.sqlite`) has one
   row per `record_note` — not two.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `workflows/agent_run.py` | The agent loop — deterministic glue |
| `workflows/queue.py` | Run queue: concurrency cap, start-rate limiter |
| `steps/llm.py` | The model step ({{ llm_sdk }}); tokens stream live, completion is checkpointed |
| `steps/tools.py` | One step per tool call, with idempotency keys |
{%- if include_hitl %}
| `steps/approval.py` | Durable human-in-the-loop wait (`DBOS.recv`) |
{%- endif %}
| `streaming.py` | Durable progress events (resumable) + live token bus |
{%- if include_api %}
| `api.py` | FastAPI: runs, SSE{% if include_hitl %}, approvals{% endif %}, a minimal inbox page at `/` |
{%- endif %}
| `agent/tools/` | Your tools — see `AGENTS.md` for the replay-safety rules |

## Following a run

{% if include_api -%}
```bash
curl -N localhost:8000/runs/<run_id>/events                    # durable progress (SSE)
curl -N -H 'Last-Event-ID: 3' localhost:8000/runs/<run_id>/events   # resume after event 3
curl -N localhost:8000/runs/<run_id>/tokens                    # live model tokens (not resumable)
```
{%- else -%}
This project has no API (`include_api = false`); use `status <run_id>`.
{%- endif %}

## Tests

`uv run pytest` runs against a throwaway SQLite system database — no Docker needed. To run
the same suite against Postgres{% if database == 'postgres' %} (`docker compose up -d`){% endif %}:

```bash
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:dbos@localhost:5432/postgres uv run pytest
```

`tests/test_resume.py` and `tests/test_idempotency.py` crash a real worker process with
`os._exit`, then recover the run in a fresh one.
{%- if database == 'lakebase' %}

## Lakebase auth

`config.py` builds a SQLAlchemy engine that fetches a Databricks OAuth token on every new
connection (pool recycled every 15 min, well inside the token lifetime). If your Databricks
App binds Lakebase as an app resource, check which `PG*` variables the platform injects and
simplify `_lakebase_engine()` accordingly.
{%- endif %}
{%- if deploy_target == 'databricks_app' %}

## Deploy to Databricks Apps

```bash
databricks bundle validate && dex run deploy
```

`databricks.yml` includes `resources/app.yml`; `app.yaml` holds the launch command. Set
secrets (model keys) as app resources, not in the bundle.
{%- endif %}

## Upgrading DBOS

`dbos` is pinned to a minor in `pyproject.toml`. Replay semantics must not shift under
in-flight runs: bump deliberately, run the crash tests, and bump `APP_VERSION` if workflow
step order changed.
